Inspire RH56 hand service

The H2 service, serial protocol helpers, DDS test client and original serial
regression tests were imported from the local dfx_inspire_service project,
an H2 adaptation of the Unitree DFX Inspire hand service. That source tree
had no Git revision metadata. Its BSD 3-Clause license is preserved here.

Original files:
  example_h2_native485.cpp
  example/hand_example.cpp
  include/SerialPort.h
  include/inspire.h
  tests/test_native485_probe.py
  tests/test_native485_dds.py

The deployment subset lives in tools/robot_services/inspire_hands/ and
tests/tools/robot_services/inspire_hands/. Integration adds an independent
build, configurable DDS domain, a read-only client default, systemd readiness
and watchdog notifications, and fault-injection checks. The older G1/H1
executables and the original machine-specific service configuration are not
distributed with this subset. Subsequent changes are recorded in Git.
